module gunbc.roadmap_forecast


data forecast_is_projection_not_observation_note: String = "A forecast projects what may happen; a CycleTimeObservation records what did happen. They are separate nominal record types with no conversion in either direction. ScheduleForecast exposes ForecastInstant and ForecastLowerBoundInterval; its epoch value is sealed inside ForecastInstant and never appears as a bare Timestamp/EpochMs observation, RoadmapAcceptanceReceipt, Signoff, or done/accepted stage. schedule_forecast derives only ScheduleForecastResult, and its refusal arm is exhaustive. Therefore a date can neither accept a roadmap node nor inhabit the observation input used to calibrate later forecasts. Estimates project; only evidence promotes."

data schedule_method_note: String = "This is a roadmap instantiation of the cited GAO critical-path and three-point-estimate methods plus the cited RCPSP work-volume lower bound, not a new scheduling vocabulary. Dependencies determine the path of longest median duration. Historical minimum/median/maximum remain an interval throughout; the small sample is never collapsed to a point. PR open-to-merge is one undecomposed observation: ReviewCycleCount and OperatorMergeLatencyAssumption remain named and visible, but ScenarioAdjustment is AdjustmentUnavailable until per-review duration and operator merge latency are separately observed. Neither is multiplied into or added onto the baseline. BeltCapacity is session-grain: under EndToEndBeltSlotOccupancyAssumption, each forecast node continuously occupies one belt slot across its modeled baseline interval, so capacity enters through ceil(total slot-time / cap). The output is explicitly conditional lower-bound projection, never a resource-leveled expected date. dissolve-on: separately grained review/merge observations, observed dispatch-to-release slot occupancy, and a grounded RCPSP resource-leveling slice replace the unavailable adjustment, declared occupancy assumption, and lower-bound-only projection; until then no consumer may read these bounds as observed labor or promised landing dates."

data remaining_cost_relative_sizing_follow_on_note: String = "FOLLOW-ON DERIVED READ, not slice 1 and never an authored field on RoadmapNode or NodeSizing: remaining-cost-to-complete-from-here is a node's own calibrated work plus the unfinished dependency closure, bucketed relative to the historical plus active task population by a separately grounded order-of-magnitude or quantile policy. It must project from this module's TotalWork and dependency-closure facts, so the label recalibrates as history accumulates and shrinks as prerequisites gain acceptance evidence. dissolve-on: a consumer needs relative portfolio sizing and grounds one population-bucketing policy; then one fold derives the label without creating a second sizing authority."

data critical_path_method_used: extdeps.project_schedule.cpm_pert.CriticalPathMethod = extdeps.project_schedule.cpm_pert.critical_path_method
data three_point_estimate_method_used: extdeps.project_schedule.cpm_pert.ThreePointEstimateMethod = extdeps.project_schedule.cpm_pert.three_point_estimate_method
data resource_capacity_lower_bound_method_used: extdeps.project_schedule.cpm_pert.ResourceCapacityLowerBoundMethod = extdeps.project_schedule.cpm_pert.resource_capacity_lower_bound_method

type SizingCell {
  intricacy: gunbc.roadmap_model.Intricacy
  volume: gunbc.roadmap_model.Volume
}

fn sizing_cell_eq(a: SizingCell, b: SizingCell) -> Bool {
  a.intricacy == b.intricacy && a.volume == b.volume
}

fn sizing_cell_of(sizing: gunbc.roadmap_model.NodeSizing) -> SizingCell? {
  match sizing {
    gunbc.roadmap_model.Unsized => Absent
    gunbc.roadmap_model.Sized { intricacy, volume, repo: _, acceptance: _ } =>
      Present { value: SizingCell { intricacy: intricacy, volume: volume } }
  }
}

type AcceptedNodePullLink {
  node: gunbc.roadmap_model.RoadmapNodeId
  pull_number: Int
}

data accepted_node_pull_link_note: String = "The business join between a durable roadmap acceptance and its implementation/acceptance pull request. Pull wire shape and its normalized timing observations stay under the single extdeps.github.pulls authority; acceptance stays in gunbc.roadmap_authority. This list says only which PR delivered an accepted node. A PR open-to-merge interval is admitted as a calibration sample only when exactly one accepted node links to that PR; a shared delivery is reported once as BundledPullDelivery and excluded because the source does not allocate its elapsed time among node sizing cells."

